  "text_pages": [
    "Student accommodation | ZHAW Zurich University of Applied Sciences\nSearch for\nDelete search term\nSearch\nStudent accommodation\nIn Winterthur, Zurich and Wädenswil, various organisations offer reasonably priced accommodation for ZHAW students. The SWOWI Foundation has the widest range and is the first place to look.\nRegular students\nIncoming students\nCross-generational\nIn Winterthur, the\nSWOWI Foundation\n(Studentischer Wohnraum Winterthur, Student Accommodation in Winterthur) offers about 280 rooms for ZHAW students.\nWOKO\n(Studentische Wohngenossenschaft Zürich, Student Housing Cooperative, Zurich) manages and runs all SWOWI properties and its own student houses in Winterthur on the Bürglistrasse 21/23 with 77 units. The Türmlihuus student dorm at Technikumstrasse 36 is also part of WOKO, but recruits its tenants itself. Livit AG also offers 105 rooms on the Untere Briggerstrasse. Ten furnished rooms in two houses (five rooms per house) are offered by \"Students Home\".\nSWOWI/WOKO accommodation\nBürglistrasse accommodation\nTürmlihuus student dorm\nStudent housing, Livit AG\nStudent housing Loge71\nStudents Home\nStudents House, Rudolf Scherrer AG\nStudent housing Tössblick\nThe\nSWOWI Foundation\noffers rooms for ZHAW students in the Wädenswil area.\nWOKO\n(Studentische Wohngenossenschaft Zürich, Student Housing Cooperative, Zurich) manages and runs the SWOWI properties.\nAnother option is the Titania Haus, which is run by a cooperative of the Titania student alumni association. You do not need to be a member of the student association to live in the Titania Haus.\nSWOWI/WOKO accommodation (accommodation in Wädenswil see Winterthur)\nTitania Haus accommodation (in German)\nFor accommodation in Zurich, please consult the following links:\nWOKO (Studentische Wohngenossenschaft Zürich)\nand\nJugendwohnnetz\n(in German).\nA number of furnished rooms at Gärtnerstrasse 4 in Winterthur and Meierhofstrasse 1/3 in Wädenswil are available for incoming students. These can be rented for six or twelve-month periods and they are managed by the\nZHAW Regis­trar’s Office\n.\nFurther offers\n­\n“Pro Senectute Kanton Zürich” organises cross-generational living arrangements, calling this “\nWohnen für Hilfe\n”(Living and Helping). Under this arrangement, older people offer students accommodation and in return, instead of money, they receive various kinds of assistance and services. The arrangement is one hour of help per month for every square metre of accommodation.\nFlyer on shared accommodation (in German only)\nFlyer on «Wohnen für Hilfe» (in German only) (PDF 1.02 MB)\nFurther information on “Wohnen für Hilfe” (in German)\nWGZimmer.ch\nRonorp.net\nmeinwgzimmer.ch\nLiving in and around Wädenswil\nstudents.ch\nFurther accommodation arrangements\nWohnangebot für Incoming Staff\nFor ZHAW incoming staff, accommodation possibilities in Winterthur and Wädenswil can be seen on the link below.\nWohnangebot für Incoming Staff\nWohnangebot für Incoming Staff\nFor ZHAW incoming staff, accommodation possibilities in Winterthur and Wädenswil can be seen on the link below.\nWohnangebot für Incoming Staff"
  ],
